name airpins
version 1.1.0-1
architecture arm64
summary "GPIO pins of the Raspberry Pi and Cubie A7S for air/OS, after pigg"
description "AirPins configures the GPIO pins of the Raspberry Pi and the Radxa Cubie A7S as inputs (with or without a pull resistor) or outputs, sets outputs (toggle or hold to invert) and shows every configured pin's level as an LED and a waveform. The pins can be laid out as on the board's headers, in GPIO order, or compactly. Configurations are pigg's .pigg files. A native Haiku version of pigg by Andrew Mackenzie and the pigg contributors; it needs the rpi_gpio driver of the air/OS Raspberry Pi 4 image or the sunxi_gpio driver of the Cubie A7S image, and simulates the pins elsewhere."
packager "air/OS contributors"
vendor "air/OS"
copyrights {
	"2026 air/OS contributors"
}
licenses {
	"MIT"
}
provides {
	airpins = 1.1.0
	app:AirPins = 1.1.0
}
requires {
	haiku >= r1~beta5
}
